# size 20x3
# Escapes that restart, and a tab measured in columns.
#
# Row 1: two escapes and a final byte. The second escape starts the sequence again and the A ends
#        it, so nothing is drawn - this used to print the A.
# Row 2: a byte that is not a character, then a tab, then a mark. The tab stop is counted in
#        columns, so the mark lands at column eight however many bytes the replacement took.
\e\eA
\e[2;1H\x81\t@
